<title>UK: Kexim prices $350 million 10-year Yankee bond.</title>
<headline>Kexim prices $350 million 10-year Yankee bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Export-Import Bank of Korea (Kexim) has priced a $350 million 10-year Yankee bond issued on Thursday, lead manager Lehman Brothers said.</p>
<p>The issue and reoffer price are 99.848, paying a semi-annual coupon of 6.50 percent with a spread of 45 basis points over the February 2004 U.S. Treasury note.</p>
<p>There is a put after seven years. The bond is due on November 15 2006. Payment date is November 20 with a short first coupon.</p>
<p>Kexim is rated A1 by Moody's and AA-minus by Standard &amp; Poor's. Fees on the deal total 5/8 percent.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
